ASE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent   # workspace root\nINPUT = BASE / \"inputs\"\nOUT = BASE / \"output\"\n\nSAMPLES = {\"sample1\": \"1\", \"sample2\": \"2\"}\nGENES_FILE = INPUT / \"differential.composition.q1.genes.txt.gz\"\nPANEL_FILE = INPUT / \"MARKER_PANEL.tsv\"\n\ndef load_counts(tag: str) -> sparse.csr_matrix:\n    path = INPUT / f\"differential.composition.q1.{tag}.mtx.gz\"\n    mat = mmread(str(path)).tocsr().astype(np.float32)  # genes x cells\n    # integrity checks\n    assert mat.min() >= 0\n    ...\n    return mat\n```\n\nHmm, mat.min() on sparse — use mat.data.min(). Integrality: np.all(np.modf(mat.data)[0] == 0).\n\nQC function:\n```python\ndef qc_stats(Xcg):  # cells x genes csr\n    lib = np.asarray(Xcg.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n    ndet = np.diff(Xcg.indptr)\n    mt_idx = ...\n```\n\nFor MT fraction: genes starting with \"MT-\". Compute per-cell MT counts with Xcg[:, mt_cols].sum(axis=1).\n\nNormalization:\n```python\ndef cp10k_log1p(Xcg, lib):\n    scale = np.zeros_like(lib)\n    nz = lib > 0\n    scale[nz] = 10000.0 / lib[nz]\n    Xn = Xcg.multiply(scale[:, None]).tocsr()\n    Xn.data = np.log1p(Xn.data)\n    return Xn\n```\n\nNote: Xcg.multiply(scale[:, None]) with scale as a 2D column (n,1) — scipy handles broadcasting. Good.\n\nScoring:\n```python\ndef marker_scores(Xn, panel, sym2idx):\n    n = Xn.shape[0]\n    T = len(panel)\n    S = np.empty((n, T), dtype=np.float64)\n    col_idx = {}\n    for t, (_, row) in enumerate(panel.iterrows()):\n        gs = row[\"markers\"].split(\",\")\n        idx = [sym2idx[g] for g in gs]\n        col_idx[row[\"cell_type\"]] = (gs, idx)\n        S[:, t] = np.asarray(Xn[:, idx].mean(axis=1)).ravel()\n    return S, col_idx\n```\n\nAssignment: lab = S.argmax(axis=1) — ties broken by first occurrence (np.argmax returns the first max). This matches panel row order.\n\nThen composition DataFrame.\n\nAlso uncertainty metrics: margin = best - second-best (sorted per row). Fraction of cells with margin < 0.1. Also per-type mean winning score.\n\nSummary JSON content: per-sample qc (n_cells, library size min/p5/median/p95/max, detected genes median, median MT%, zero-library cell count, integrality check passed), assignment statistics, depletion analysis including full ratio table, and per-type mean winning score and margin statistics.\n\nWrite out composition.csv, depleted_call.json, analysis_summary.json.\n\nRounding for CSV: fraction to 6 decimals. n_cells as int.\n\nDepletion call JSON: keep full precision (float), maybe round to 6 digits for readability.\n\nThen report.md: write it after seeing the summary. Include:\n- Objective and inputs\n- Methods: QC (documentation only; frozen rule forbids filtering), normalization CP10K+log1p, marker scoring per ANNOTATION_RULE.md, tie-break, denominator\n- QC results table\n- Composition table (both samples) with ratios\n- Rationale for annotation: counts, mean marker scores, top types\n- Depletion call + rationale\n- Uncertainty and limitations\n\nThen an independent validation script (temporary, not a deliverable):\n- Read CSV, check sums\n- Independently recompute the marker sum of the depleted type in sample 2 vs sample 1 by a different method (e.g., dense marker submatrix, computing library size with np.add.reduceat on indptr) and confirm direction.\n- Confirm that the argmin ratio from the CSV matches the JSON.\n\nNow let me create the output directory and write analysis.py."}}
