with W[g,t] = 1/k_t if gene g is a marker of type t. Score = Xn @ W (cells × types). Then argmax. This is mathematically equivalent, but computed via a different code path (sparse matrix-matrix product rather than per-type slicing).\n\nLibrary size via CSC: mat_csc = mat.tocsc(); lib = np.add.reduceat(mat_csc.data, mat_csc.indptr[:-1])… note: for cells × genes CSR, row sums are better computed via np.add.reduceat(Xcg.data, Xcg.indptr[:-1]) (with handling for empty rows). Use this (different from .sum(axis=1)).\n\nAlso, verify that the header dimensions parsed from the gz file match.\n\nLet me write _verify.py (temporary file, workspace root — it's within the workspace so it's permitted; delete afterwards, or leave it? Deliverables are inside output/; to keep the workspace clean I'll delete it later, but the task requires working only inside the workspace — a temporary file is fine. I'll delete it after running)."}}
